  "description": "A time-lane diagram: Party A's lane and Party B's lane, the supplied order running down both. The proposal (●) and the withdrawal message (◆) each travel on their own solid line from A's lane to B's lane; the sent and received events are marked on the lanes with their fictional time labels in the supplied order, so the lines cross when the order supplied says so. Only the supplied relationships are drawn and captioned (communication, relation, sequence; causal only when supplied); a tracer follows the supplied traversal order, the focus element swells, and the cards gather toward B's lane. No effect of the order is inferred.",
